BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:American Devotion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T120000
UID:blogto-229182@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/01/14/original_image3083111f-99af-4728-8ab2-639a67932a
 ba.jpg
DESCRIPTION:American Devotion takes us back to 1957 and the Connecticut fa
 rmhouse shared by Marilyn Monroe and her celebrated playwright husband\, A
 rthur Miller. In this fictional version of events\, Norman Mailer has succ
 essfully wangled a coveted invitation for cocktails with the reclusive cou
 ple.  With McCarthyism running rampant\, Miller has been called to testify
  before the House of Un-American Activities Committee adding further strai
 n to an already besieged marriage.  Mailer storms into this delicate situa
 tion ready to do battle and claim his prize at any cost but Monroe has pla
 ns of her own for the evening's festivities.
LOCATION:Streetcar Crowsnest Studio Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/american-devotion-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Oil Painting Experience by Artbox
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T220000
UID:blogto-235405@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/22/original_image2cb3ce60-b9c2-4e38-967c-20f1e8d181
 1f.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a guided oil painting workshop where you’ll expl
 ore the rich colour\, softness\, and depth of oil paint.\nWhat to Expect:\
 nPerfect for both beginners and those refining their practice\, this works
 hop guides you step-by-step through sketching\, layering\, blending\, and 
 building highlights and shadows to create realism and vibrancy. You’ll l
 earn time-honoured oil painting techniques with supportive guidance throug
 hout.\nGuided Instruction:\nLearn foundational oil painting methods from a
 n experienced artist—from initial sketch to final detail work—using la
 yering\, glazing\, and observation of light.\nCreative Freedom: Customize 
 your painting with your own tones\, brushwork style\, and level of realism
  or looseness.\nAll Materials Included: High-quality oil paints\, brushes\
 , palette knives\, apron\, stretched canvas\, to-go box\, and all other ne
 cessary supplies are included.\nRelaxed Studio Atmosphere: Enjoy a relaxed
 \, inspiring space with soft music and uplifting creative energy.\nSnacks 
 & Refreshments: Complimentary coffee\, tea\, water and snacks available th
 roughout.\nWho Should Join:\nSuitable for beginners and intermediate artis
 ts.\nMust be ages 12+. Participants under 18 must be accompanied by a payi
 ng 18+ adult.\nLimited spots available — reserve your canvas today.\nSee
  more events at: https://www.artboxstudiogallery.com/calendar\nCall us at:
  647-617-9550
LOCATION:Artbox Studio Gallery
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/an-oil-painting-experience-by-artbox-tor
 onto-13/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Clothing Swap & Stitch Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T203000
UID:blogto-234972@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/13/original_image2be690f9-9e9e-4d60-a93b-5e7cc880be
 25.jpg
DESCRIPTION:​Join us for an evening of swapping\, stitching\, and social
 izing as part of Toronto Climate Week! This isn’t your typical clothing 
 swap because we believe building community and sharing skills are also ess
 ential aspects of a circular economy.\n​For the clothing swap\, we sugge
 st bringing about 10 items (clothes\, shoes\, or accessories)\, preferably
  seasonal items\, clean and in good condition - think something you’d be
  happy to receive! Any items leftover at the end of the swap will be donat
 ed to New Circles.\n​For the mending lab\, we encourage you to bring an 
 item or two in need of minor repair\, perhaps a sock that needs darning\, 
 a button that needs to be reattached or jeans requiring a small patch. If 
 you find something at the swap that needs a small adjustment\, we may be a
 ble to help with that too!
LOCATION:CSI Spadina
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/clothing-swap-stitch-social-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
