 gto.com/events/2026/06/02/original_image6f12eecc-0b47-4c58-917c-609286746a
 56.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Escape the hustle and bustle of the city and discover one of D
 owntown Yonge’s hidden gems. Tucked behind CF Toronto Eaton Centre\, Tri
 nity Square Park transforms into a vibrant summer gathering space filled w
 ith free activities\, public art\, markets\, workshops\, and opportunities
  to relax and recharge.\nWhether you’re taking a lunch break\, meeting f
 riends\, exploring public art\, or simply looking for a quiet place to unw
 ind\, there’s always something new to discover throughout the season.\nF
 eatured Summer Programming\n- Pyramid Fields by Cyril Lancelin: June 3–2
 8 | 9AM–9PM (Part of Luminato Festival)\n- Artist Talk with Cyril Lancel
 in: June 3 | 4:30PM–5PM (Part of Luminato Festival)\n- Pride Market: Fir
 st three weekends in June | 12PM–6PM\n- Photography Workshop: June 11 | 
 12PM–1PM\n- Watercolour Painting Sessions: June 18\; July 2 & 16\; Augus
 t 6 & 20 | 10AM–4PM\n- Farmer’s Market: July 9\, 16\, 23 & 30\; August
  6\, 13 & 20 | 11:30AM–2PM\n📍 Trinity Square Park (19 Trinity Sq.)\n
 📅 June – August 2026\nWebsite: https://downtownyonge.com/summer/trini
 tysquare/
LOCATION:Trinity Square Park
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/take-a-break-trinity-square-park-toronto
 /
