 gto.com/events/2026/05/21/original_image56bcd9f5-8b3e-42d8-a5ef-099c2dbd08
 cc.jpg
DESCRIPTION:How do you know if the health information you are reading onli
 ne is actually true?\nJoin us for an engaging talk on healthy aging with D
 r. Milena Head\, Professor of Information Systems at McMaster University\,
  as she explores the science behind online misinformation and shares pract
 ical strategies to help you evaluate what you can trust.\nIn a world full 
 of health advice\, tips\, and quick fixes\, it can be difficult to separat
 e facts from fiction. This session will help you feel more confident and i
 nformed when navigating health information online\, especially in relation
  to your wellbeing and healthy aging.
LOCATION:Toronto Public Library
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/snacks-science-toronto-3/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
