BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A 40th Anniversary Celebration of Charles Atlas' "Hail The New Pur
 itan"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T220000
UID:blogto-235519@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/25/original_image9cc849b4-ca4f-429a-b7d6-ffc3f13d5e
 82.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Directed by Charles Atlas and featuring the work of Scottish c
 horeographer Michael Clark\, Hail The New Puritan is a fictionalized docum
 entary capturing the rare intersection of ballet technique\, punk aestheti
 c\, and queer subculture that defined Clark’s groundbreaking work in the
  1980s.\nWith Leigh Bowery in charge of costumes\, Trojan contributing to 
 set design\, and The Fall behind the soundtrack\, Hail The New Puritan is 
 more than a dance film\, it is a portrait of a radical artistic moment tha
 t reshaped how contemporary dance could exist within popular and undergrou
 nd culture.\nTo celebrate the 40th anniversary of this trailblazing film\,
  the evening will include:\n🕺”hey it was nice knowing you”\, a live
  dance performance by DOLLHEAD 2000 (aka TDT’s Bray Cairns and Roberto S
 oria)\n🎓 Introduction by Amelia Ehrhardt from Weird Ballet\n🎞️ Fea
 ture screening of Hail the New Puritan\n(dir. Charles Atlas\, UK\, 1986\, 
 85 min)
LOCATION:Winchester Street Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/a-40th-anniversary-celebration-of-charle
 s-atlas-hail-the-new-puritan-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
