BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Reclaiming the Light Within - FREE Ultimate Soul-Affirming Virtual
  Retreat for Women Healing from Trauma
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T223000
UID:blogto-235942@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/02/original_imagebc69516f-9ac4-493a-8e09-788471fea4
 c0.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This is an immersive virtual healing experience for the woman 
 who is holding it all together on the outside — but knows something deep
 er isn’t fully working underneath.\nYou don’t need a diagnosis for thi
 s to be real. What you’ve been through doesn’t just live in your past 
 —it lives in your body. And those patterns don’t just disappear. They 
 show up in how you think\, respond under pressure\, relate to others\, or 
 shut down. Every. Single. Day.\nIf you’re honest…you don’t just feel
  stressed. You feel wired\, exhausted\, and stuck in patterns you can’t 
 think your way out of.\nThis free event is designed to be a safe\, support
 ive space — a sanctuary for real\, embodied healing. This is somatic\, t
 rauma-informed work\, which means we go to the place where these patterns 
 actually live. In your body.\nYou won’t be asked to relive your past. Yo
 u won’t be pushed or overwhelmed.  Instead\, you’ll be guided gently t
 o safely experience and shift what’s underneath — in a way that feels 
 grounded\, supported\, and deeply real.\nThis isn’t surface-level coachi
 ng. It’s the kind of work that creates real\, embodied change… because
  you don’t just understand something new.\nThere’s something powerful 
 about choosing yourself on a Friday night — not to escape…but to meet 
 yourself at a deeper level.\nTo release what your body has been holding…
 and reclaim the power that was never actually lost. In a room full of wome
 n doing the same. This is where you stop surviving…This is where you ris
 e.\nIf your body is already saying yes… trust that. Join us at 7pm ET on
  Friday\, June 5th. Save your spot here and the zoom link will be emailed 
 to you:\nhttp://www.reclaimingthelightwithin.com\nPRIZE GIVEAWAY!!!!!\nOne
  woman who attends live will win a PRIZE valued at $600 USD! You need to b
 e in the Zoom room to qualify. If you are a woman recovering from trauma\,
  you will not want to miss this.
LOCATION:Virtual Event
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/reclaiming-the-light-within-free-ultimat
 e-soul-affirming-virtual-retreat-for-women-healing-from-trauma-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shrimp Daddy Comedy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T214500
UID:blogto-235795@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/30/original_image4c0a613f-4a77-427e-8f5f-2b82971dff
 38.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for a one night memorable event with Canada's funnie
 st headliners and featuring special guests. You miss this\, you’ve misse
 d out!\nFeaturing:\nFARAZ NIAFATTAH\nFaraz Niafattah is an up-and-coming c
 omedian who is making waves in the Toronto scene with his sharp deadpan de
 livery and effortlessly relatable humor. He performs at comedy clubs acros
 s Canada and has been featured at top festivals such as Just For Laughs To
 ronto\, Vail Comedy Festival in Colorado\, Limestone Comedy Festival in In
 diana\, San Francisco Sketchfest\, The Haymaker Comedy Festival in Prince 
 Edward County\, and Hubcap Comedy Festival in Moncton. His comedy has been
  showcased with Don’t Tell Comedy in Toronto and Montreal\, and heard na
 tionally on CBC’s Laugh Out Loud. Recognized as one of the most exciting
  new voices in Canadian comedy\, Faraz will release his debut comedy speci
 al later this year.\n@gypsytears69\nHISHAM KELATI\nHisham Kelati is a Toro
 nto-based standup comedian and writer known for his vivid and engaging sto
 rytelling. He is a 2022 Juno nominee for Best Comedy Album of the Year for
  his debut release Tigre King. He performed at Just for Laughs as part of 
 the New Faces showcase in 2019\, and that same year he was nominated for B
 est Taped Performance at the Canadian Comedy Awards\, and won Host of the 
 Year at the Toronto Comedy Awards.\nHisham has opened for Saturday Night L
 ive's Chris Redd\, and WTF Podcast host Marc Maron. He’s performed on CB
 C Radio’s Accent on Toronto and CBC’s The Debaters\, has written for C
 BC's hit sketch show TallBoyz\, and can currently be seen on CBC's The New
  Wave of Stand-up and CTV’s The Stand Up Show with Jon Dore! He can also
  be heard on his food and comedy podcast Bites and Bits on The Sonar Netwo
 rk.\n@hishamkelati\nJORDAN POLICICCHIO\nJordan Policicchio recently finish
 ed a 15-city cross Canada comedy tour with Abbas Wahab and has opened for 
 Che Durena at New York Comedy Club. He is one of Canada’s fastest rising
  club regulars and features at Absolute Comedy\, The Corner Comedy Club an
 d was just added to Yuk Yuk’s Rising Stars roster. His quick-wit and rel
 atable material make him a must-see act.\n@jordanpolicicchio\nRAHUL TOPIWA
 LA\nRahul Topiwala has been performing stand-up comedy for eight years\, b
 ringing sharp wit and relatable storytelling to stages across Canada. He b
 egan his comedy journey in university alongside some funny professors and 
 has since performed in three different countries. A featured performer at 
 Just For Laughs and the Departures Comedy Festival\, he’s a regular at t
 op clubs in Toronto and Ottawa\, where he shares his hilarious takes on cu
 lture\, countries\, and married life.\n@rrahultopiwala\nHANNAH LAWRENCE\nH
 annah Lawrence is a stand-up comedian from Toronto. Since moving to the UK
  less than a year ago\, she’s been a televised semi-finalist in the BBC 
 New Comedy Awards and she’s performed at the Women in Comedy Festival. H
 er humor has graced the stages at renowned events such as Just For Laughs 
 Toronto\, The Edinburgh Fringe Festival and The NXNE Festival. Her stand u
 p has featured on CBC and Sirius XM\, and she is the recipient of the Davi
 d Goodman award for Comedic Excellence. Her debut album\, “Two Girls Liv
 e” streams across platforms throughout North America.\n@hlawrencee\nMARK
  EDWARDS\nMark Robert Edwards was born in Toronto\, Canada. After graduati
 ng from Lawrence Park Collegiate Institute\, he studied comedy writing and
  performance at Humber College in Etobicoke\, Ontario\, under the tutelage
  of such people as Robin Duke (SNL\, SCTV).\nIn 2012\, Mark was cast in Ni
 ckelodeon's Rocket Monkeys\, for which he was nominated for a Canadian Scr
 een Award (CSA). He was soon hired as a writer\, and continued to write an
 d voice many characters for Nickelodeon\, Cartoon Network\, YTV\, and Tele
 toon\, earning two more CSA nominations.\nEarly in 2022\, Mark began posti
 ng short sketches and impressions on social media\, amassing more than 500
 k followers across platforms and garnering over 100 million views.\n@someg
 uymark\nAND SPECIAL GUESTS!
LOCATION:Comedy Bar
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/shrimp-daddy-comedy-toronto-24/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
