BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Silk Painting Workshop with Alek Phan
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T160000
UID:blogto-235547@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/26/original_image45fe7394-ad0f-4cbc-9258-f6598887ba
 fb.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an artist-led silk painting workshop this MOCA Com
 munity Weekend!\nIn this hands-on workshop\, you’ll be introduced to the
  materials and processes of Vietnamese silk painting\, a tradition where t
 he movement of pigment across fabric reflects patience\, balance\, and sen
 sitivity to the natural flow of water. Guided by artist and educator Phan 
 Trúc (Alek)\, you’ll explore how pigment\, water\, and silk interact to
  create soft layers of colour and light.\nInspired by the traditional text
 iles and the meditative\, quiet power of making explored in Kimsooja’s e
 xhibition “Dimensions of a Needle\,” the workshop explores the ways te
 xtiles can hold cultural histories\, stories\, and memories.\nNo prior exp
 erience is required\, though an artistic background or previous experience
  can be helpful. Make a day of it and start with Alek Phan’s presentatio
 n: “Cross Cultural Practice in Contemporary Art. “
LOCATION:MOCA Toronto
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/silk-painting-workshop-with-alek-phan-to
 ronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
