 f3.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Step into the spotlight for an unforgettable evening of music\
 , storytelling\, and the magic of the theatre. A Night On Broadway celebra
 tes the dazzle of live performance through familiar choral works inspired 
 by the energy and emotion of Broadway’s greatest moments.\nFeaturing 100
  Years of Broadway arr. Mac Huff\, a medley that moves from spectacular sh
 owstoppers to moments of beauty and reflection\, and captures the heart of
  musical theatre through vibrant harmonies and expressive storytelling.\nI
 n the Forest composed by Kaleb Hikele and arranged by Univox Artistic Dire
 ctor Cody MacFarlane will also be performed.\nJoin us for an evening where
  the lights shine bright\, the music soars\, and every voice takes centre 
 stage.\nFeaturing:\n- Malcolm Cody MacFarlane\, Artistic Director\n- Kevin
  Stolz\, Piano\n- Univox Choir\nTickets:\n- $30\, $35 with a $5 donation t
 o the the choir\, or $40 with a $10 donation to the choir\n- Online pre-sa
 le and at the Door\n- Children 12 and under are free\n- Cash and Card acce
 pted\nIntermission will include a Bake Sale with donations supporting the 
 choir.\nUnivox Choir is a registered charity and relies on the generous su
 pport of our community to ensure we can continue to bring people together 
 and create music that inspires\, educates and challenges singers\, audienc
 e members and the wider community. Donations allow Univox to expand our mu
 sical offerings\, bring in guest artists and musicians\, and perform at di
 fferent venues across the city.\nIf you know one of our choristers\, have 
 enjoyed one of our concerts\, or want to support a growing arts organizati
 on\, please consider donating to Vox Choirs either with an enhanced ticket
  purchase or through CanadaHelps!\nFor more information\, please visit www
 .voxchoirs.com or follow @VoxChoirs on social media.\nNOTES:\n- Online tic
 ket sales will end 2 hours before the start of the concert (5pm ET). Ticke
 ts are still available for purchase at the door by cash or card.\n- The ve
 nue is wheelchair accessible.\n- COVID-19 Protocols: Univox Choir is follo
 wing all Health Canada\, Public Health Ontario\, and Toronto Public Health
  guidelines. As government\, organization\, and venue guidelines evolve\, 
 so may these safety measures. Visit this page or www.voxchoirs.com for up-
 to-date information.
LOCATION:Christ Church Deer Park
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/univox-choir-presents-a-night-on-broadwa
 y-toronto/
