BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Breakthrough T1D Walk - Together we Walk for a future free from ty
 pe 1 diabetes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260607T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260607T120000
UID:blogto-235900@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/02/original_imageef88ecf9-5cc0-45ac-8420-033cf2898c
 a7.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Breakthrough T1D™ Walk is the largest fundraising event in C
 anada that unites the type 1 diabetes (T1D) community in support of the cl
 ose to 300\,000 Canadians with T1D.\nPeople with T1D must constantly monit
 or blood glucose levels and take external insulin\, either by pump\, multi
 ple daily injections or pen to stay alive. And even with the most vigilant
  management\, there are risks of potentially life-altering complications. 
 T1D is a relentless autoimmune disease - that has no cure\, yet.\nThe Walk
  is one of the longest standing and most successful fundraising events in 
 the country and has a fundraising goal of more than $3 million from Walks 
 held across Canada.\nThis is more than a Walk\, it’s a movement to end T
 1D.\nWhat: 	Breakthrough T1D Walk\nWhen:  	Sunday\, June 7\, 2026\nTime:
    	Registration Opens: 9:00AM EDT\nOpening Ceremony: 10:30AM EDT\nWal
 k Starts: 11:00AM EDT\nWhere: 	E.T. Seton Park\, 73 Thorncliffe Park Dr.
 \nWho:   	Jessica Diniz\, President and CEO\, Breakthrough T1D Canada\
 nBreakthrough T1D Youth Ambassador\, Hunter\, age 10\, diagnosed with T1D 
 at age 9\nMax Domi\, NHL Player\, Breakthrough T1D Spokesperson\, diagnose
 d with T1D at age 12
LOCATION:E.T. Seton Park
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/breakthrough-t1d-walk-together-we-walk-f
 or-a-future-free-from-type-1-diabetes-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
