 4c.jpg
DESCRIPTION:ABOUT THE SHOW\nExperience the raw\, wild\, and deeply improvi
 sational nature of flamenco at Toronto's historic venue\, the Monarch Tave
 rn. Acoustic and unamplified\, come see flamenco at its purest\, most inte
 nse and most thrilling. Modelled off the flamenco tablaos in Granada\, nes
 tled into caves in the city's hillside\, this is flamenco as it is perform
 ed in Spain: improvised and dynamic.\nLet everything else slip away and ex
 perience flamenco as it is rarely seen outside of Spain. Learn about the h
 istory of flamenco\, all while sipping on wine and tasting specially prepa
 red tapas.\nTHIS MONTH'S PERFORMERS - TO BE ANNOUNCED!\nTIME\nDoors open a
 t 7pm\nShow starts at 8pm\nCome early to get the best seat! Stay for the f
 lamenco party at the end.\nSORRY\, no refunds!\nMORE INFO\nFabcollab.ca
LOCATION:The Monarch Tavern
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/la-cueva-flamenco-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
