ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/14/original_image5dcb0048-7246-46f0-be08-59ef514079
 83.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Looking for a Pride experience that’s a little more relaxed\
 , a little more green\, and full of good energy? Join us for an afternoon 
 celebration that blends live music\, nature\, and community in a beautiful
  garden setting—perfect for first-time visitors and longtime garden love
 rs alike.\nDrop in anytime to experience Pride at your own pace. Stretch o
 ut on the lawn with a picnic blanket (bring your own or borrow one of ours
 )\, enjoy a curated line up of Queer music artists\, and connect with frie
 nds and chosen family in an open\, welcoming space.\nWhat to Expect:\nLive
  Music + Sofar Sounds: A series of intimate outdoor performances with surp
 rise queer musical guests.\nQueer Plant Swap: Bring plants\, cuttings\, or
  seeds to trade. Take a to the swap table when you arrive and take ticket 
 swap. If you don’t find something right away and come back to discover s
 omething new as new people and plants arrive.\nTITA at Our Garden: Spend t
 ime with TITA (she/they)\, your Filipina Auntie\, exploring queer plants\,
  self-expression\, and the joy of drag.\nSparkle Bloom Bar: Stop by and ge
 t blinged up and bloom with pride. Connect with circus fairies who will be
 dazzle your look with glitter\, gems\, and fresh floral hair accents.\nFoo
 d + Drinks: Visit the Dandelion Café for picnic fare\, light bites\, and 
 refreshing drinks.\nCommunity Partners + Free Family Activities: Drop-in t
 o the Children’s Centre for themed make and take crafting.\nThis event i
 s supported by the City of Toronto’s Music Office.
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/pride-at-the-garden-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
