BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Emerging Creators Unit Showcase 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T220000
UID:blogto-235333@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/21/original_image87685e73-f9e0-4750-9f35-93649fb374
 a0.jpg
DESCRIPTION:June 9\, 2026 // Doors 6:30PM Show 7:30PM // In the Chamber\nT
 ickets $10 – $75 + fees\nAll season long\, our Emerging Creators Unit ha
 s been forging a path of artistic discovery. At Queer Pride\, participants
  Dae Conrod\, Tyler Cunningham\, and Lili Robinson conclude their time wit
 h a sharing of newly developed work and insights into their creative proce
 sses and learnings.\nDae Conrod\, Tyler Cunningham\, Lili Robinson // ECU 
 participants\nAmanda Cordner // ECU director\nThe Emerging Creators Unit i
 s an artist-driven\, mentor-supported creative model for strongly motivate
 d emerging queer and/or trans artists\, facilitated this year by artist Am
 anda Cordner. The Emerging Creators Unit offers an intensive opportunity t
 o develop your artistic practice and producing skills. Artists are invited
  to apply with a project — or a seed of a project — that will serve as
  a vehicle to advance their artistic practice.\nFeaturing:\nDae Conrod is 
 a white\, trans multi-disciplinary artist living in Tkaronto by way of Mi'
 kma'ki. They are a writer\, actor\, nap enthusiast\, and abolitionist. The
 y are grateful for the many opportunities for growth and exploration they
 ’ve had at places like Sheridan College\, The Second City Toronto\, and 
 Neptune Theatre. As well as the people they’ve had the pleasure of explo
 ring with\, including the Liberation Practice Field and The Bus Stop Theat
 re Cooperative (Kjipuktuk). They believe love is a revolutionary force and
  hope to remind you of that through their work and presence. They hope you
  laugh with beloveds today.\nTyler (he/they) is addicted to ASMR slime vid
 eos but is also a performance artist. Across Canada and Europe\, Tyler has
  collaborated with other artists and spirits to create performances\, audi
 o walks\, music theater\, and installations that have taken them to the ru
 ins of city walls\, playgrounds\, experimental music venues\, the Atlantic
  Ocean\, sex clubs\, and bathrooms stalls. Lately\, Tyler has enjoyed wear
 ing inflatable elephant costumes. He is overjoyed to be making his Buddies
  Debut as a member of the 2026 ECU Cohort!\nLili Robinson is a Black queer
  creator with political transformation and collective healing central to t
 heir work. They draw from lineages of Afrofuturism\, Black horror\, and Bl
 ack Feminism to get at the things that haunt and the things that are hard 
 to talk about. Companies/programs she’s worked with include: the Cultch\
 , the Arts Club\, Rumble Theatre\, Theatre Replacement\, Neworld Theatre\,
  Queer Arts Festival\, rEvolver Festival\, Obsidian Theatre\, Crossroads T
 heatre\, and the Banff Playwrights Lab. Her award-winning play\, Mx\, laid
  the groundwork for the murky\, genderbendy neobouffon clown world she’l
 l be returning to with reap. This is Lili’s Buddies debut.\nThe Emerging
  Creators Unit Showcase is part of Buddies Queer Pride 2026. Visit buddies
 inbadtimes.com/pride for all events and shows.
LOCATION:Buddies in Bad Times
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/emerging-creators-unit-showcase-2026-tor
 onto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
