BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Achillean Blood On the Clocktower at Super Bargain Bar in Cabbaget
 own
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T210000
UID:blogto-235720@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/28/original_image97af6db9-44b2-40ba-adb9-b7ee04643e
 94.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Whether you're a seasoned gamer or new to the world of social 
 deception games\, this event offers something for everyone. Come solo or w
 ith friends and immerse yourself in a game of Blood on the Clocktower. Our
  events are a great way to connect with members of local communities and a
 re perfect for folks arriving in Toronto looking to make new connections.\
 nWhat is Blood on the Clocktower? - Blood on the Clocktower is an advanced
  version of the game Werewolf\, where crucially\, the dead still have an i
 mportant role to play in the game. The game is run by a Storyteller who ha
 s carefully crafted an experience and facilitates the game for up to 20 pl
 ayers. It is part deduction and part deception. Set in the town of Ravensw
 ood Bluff\, players in the game assume different roles\, each with unique 
 abilities to hunt down evil or manipulate the townsfolk.\nThanks to the ge
 nerosity of Super Bargain Bar\, we will have plenty of space for the night
  to engage in the social deduction of Blood on the Clocktower. Super Barga
 in has a menu with both alcoholic and nonalcoholic beverages that you can 
 order from while we’re having fun deducing and deceiving. Tickets for th
 is event are $20 or $13.50 for Changeling Special Events Members.\nWhereve
 r you are on the achillean spectrum\, you are invited to join us!\nIf you 
 have not played before or are newer to the game\, there will be a quick tu
 torial at the top of the event to learn how to play and ask any questions 
 from the Storyteller.\nWe will be playing the classic beginner script Trou
 ble Brewing at this event.\nAge recommendation\, 16 years +\nTo learn more
 \, find Changeling Gaming Events Toronto on Eventbrite or click the websit
 e link to see this event (see right side on desktop/above on mobile).
LOCATION:Super Bargain
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/achillean-blood-on-the-clocktower-at-sup
 er-bargain-bar-in-cabbagetown-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Movie Night before the World Cup - Eye Contact
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T200000
UID:blogto-235482@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/25/original_image698fcc5f-3e84-4a2b-a6a8-7211b93994
 13.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special screening of the documentary Eye Contact
  before the FIFA World Cup 2026™!\nOnce every four years\, the internati
 onal Deaf Olympics\, or Deaflympics\, are held for athletes who are Deaf o
 r hard of hearing. This documentary follows Japan’s first Deaf women’s
  soccer team to compete in the Games\, and was screened at the 2010 Taiwan
  International Documentary Festival and Russia’s International Disabilit
 y Film Festival\, “Breaking Down Barriers.” Japan’s Deaf women’s s
 occer team qualified to participate in the 2009 Summer Deaflympics held in
  Taipei. Hailing from different professions and age brackets\, the women b
 and together in preparation for the match. Making a name for themselves\, 
 however\, is no easy task. Learning from their experiences\, they move for
 ward with a positive attitude.\nDoors open 6:00PM | Film Screening | In-Pe
 rson | JFT Event Hall\nDirected by NAKAMURA Kazuhiko • 2010 • Document
 ary • 88 minutes • Presented in Japanese\, Japanese Sign Language & Ja
 panese Simu-Com Sign Language with English subtitles
LOCATION:Japan Foundation Toronto
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/free-movie-night-before-the-world-cup-ey
 e-contact-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
