BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Twin Sues:  A New Canadian Play Borders\, Power\, Friendship
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T210000
UID:blogto-235448@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/23/original_imagedb0f2941-13d7-441b-a1fe-26fc4e0adb
 ac.jpg
DESCRIPTION:STEP INTO THE WORLD OF THE TWIN SUES\nA new Canadian play by a
 ward-winning playwright Garrett M. Ryan\nIn the middle of a fictional Amer
 ican-Canadian war\, the twin cities of Sault Ste. Marie have been annexed 
 and forced back together under a single rule. The border is gone. The syst
 em remains.\nAt the centre of it all: two women. Same name. Same past. Ver
 y different present.\nSue Johnson and Sue Jackson\, once inseparable\, kno
 wn as the “Twin Sues”\, now stand on opposite sides of something they 
 no longer fully understand\, sharing control of a checkpoint on a newly na
 tionalized bridge. What used to divide them has disappeared. What still bi
 nds them… is harder to escape.\nWhat begins as routine slips\, slowly an
 d quietly\, into something else. Power lingers. Roles calcify. And the que
 stion of who belongs\, where\, and to what\, refuses to go away.\nTold thr
 ough a darkly comic\, documentary-style lens\, The Twin Sues is sharp\, un
 settling\, and unexpectedly human. It’s about borders\, but also about f
 riendship\, identity\, and the systems we inherit long after they’ve sto
 pped making sense.\nDr. Strangelove meets Corner Gas\, with the absurdity 
 of The Death of Stalin.\n-June 10th-14th\n-The Assembly Theatre\, Toronto\
 nLimited capacity. Intimate space. Don’t wait\, this is the kind of show
  people talk about after they’ve seen it.
LOCATION:The Assembly Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-twin-sues-a-new-canadian-play-border
 s-power-friendship-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:THINKING BEYOND THE MARKET: A Film About Genuinely Affordable Hous
 ing
