BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Celebrate the launch of Nowhere with Jon Claytor and special guest
 s!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T200000
UID:blogto-235608@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/27/original_image296425af-b485-44d5-93c2-f20122e3da
 2f.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Come and celebrate the launch of Nowhere with Jon Claytor and 
 special guests\, Ian Roy and José Contreras! This event is free and open 
 to the public.\nA hilarious and sinister reflection on growing up in a wor
 ld where monsters are real\, Nowhere is a dreamlike meditation on adolesce
 nce and the absurdity of small-town life. Jon will be reading from this un
 forgettable graphic novel\, Ian will be reading from his brand new short s
 tory collection\, Astrid\, Aghast\, and singer-songwriter José will play 
 a short set and musical accompaniment to the evening’s readings.\nAbout 
 the Authors:\nJON CLAYTOR is a graphic novelist\, painter\, and writer. Bo
 rn in San Francisco\, he lived and worked in several Canadian cities\, inc
 luding Halifax\, Vancouver\, Montreal\, and Toronto\, before settling in S
 ackville\, New Brunswick. Claytor’s work ranges from oil painting and wa
 tercolour to comics. He has had solo exhibitions at galleries in Montreal\
 , Toronto\, Los Angeles\, and throughout the Maritimes. He has also writte
 n and illustrated stories for CBC Radio\, the Frye Festival\, and the webs
 ite ruralharmreduction.com.\nIAN ROY is a writer\, screen printer\, and ed
 ucator. His work has appeared in numerous magazines and journals\, includi
 ng The Antigonish Review\, Arc\, Geist\, Long Con Magazine\, Maisonneuve\,
  and The New Quarterly. Ian is the author of six books\, including the sho
 rt story collection\, People Leaving\, which was short-listed for both the
  City of Ottawa Book Award and the Upper Canada Writers’ Craft Award.
LOCATION:Flying Books
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/celebrate-the-launch-of-nowhere-with-jon
 -claytor-and-special-guests-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
