BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Les Bandes Portage
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T230000
UID:blogto-235670@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/28/original_image6509d73c-2e0c-4435-8b5a-32344ef719
 55.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Les Bandes Portage is a fundraising concert supporting Project
  Canoe\, a Toronto-based nonprofit that has been sending youth facing barr
 iers\, ages 13-18\, on backcountry canoe trips and urban outdoor experienc
 es since 1977. Time in nature builds confidence\, resilience\, and mental 
 wellbeing — and every young person deserves access to that\, regardless 
 of what barriers stand in their way.\nThe music of the night kicks off at 
 7:30 PM with Drunk Robot — a Toronto alt-rock cover band known for high-
 energy sets and just enough chaos to keep things interesting. Headlining l
 ater in the night is Generator X\, a six-piece tribute to the golden era o
 f alt-rock\, pop-punk\, and post-grunge (think 1995–2005)\, delivering t
 he dual guitars and nostalgic attitude that makes those songs feel as loud
  and alive as ever.\nBetween sets\, try your luck at the raffle for prizes
  including Blue Jays tickets\, two passes to the AGO\, a pair of Blundston
 e boots\, a Niagara Nautico sailing charter credit\, a zipline and aerial 
 trek experience\, a 2-hour canoe rental\, and more.\n\nDoors open at 7:00 
 PM. Tickets are $20.
LOCATION:Junction Underground
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/les-bandes-portage-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Magician Chris Ramsay: It's Probably Nothing Tour with Special Com
 edian Guest Dave Foley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T220000
UID:blogto-235860@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/01/original_image357cdd32-e7c5-4508-9f3a-661674df39
 17.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Internationally acclaimed magician\, podcaster\, and Canadian 
 YouTube creator Chris Ramsay brings his It’s Probably Nothing  14-city t
 our to Toronto on June 11 at The Danforth Music Hall. Featuring special gu
 est\, legendary Canadian actor and comedian Dave Foley\, the immersive liv
 e podcast theatre experience explores UFOs\, unexplained phenomena\, consc
 iousness\, forgotten history\, and the mysteries that continue to fascinat
 e audiences around the world.\nCo-hosted alongside journalist and Discover
 y Channel’s Alien Encounters: Fact or Fiction personality Chrissy Newton
 \, the one-night-only Toronto event blends live conversation\, storytellin
 g\, audience testimony\, investigation\, and theatrical surprises into an 
 experience that evolves differently each night.\nThe Toronto event arrives
  during a period of unprecedented mainstream attention surrounding UFOs an
 d unidentified aerial phenomena (UAP). Recent developments have included t
 he release of more than 200 UFO-related files by the Trump administration\
 , ongoing speculation surrounding additional classified disclosures\, and 
 growing public fascination fueled by media\, entertainment\, and political
  discussion.\nIt’s Probably Nothing examines how UAP conversations have 
 shifted from fringe speculation to mainstream culture\, influencing entert
 ainment\, comedy\, social media\, government transparency discussions\, an
 d public curiosity about the unknown.\nThe evening will explore:\n- UFO/UA
 P disclosure and government transparency\n- Consciousness and unexplained 
 experiences\n- Strange coincidences and audience testimonies\n- The role o
 f media and pop culture in shaping belief\n- Why fascination with the unex
 plained continues to grow globally\nVenue: The Danforth Music Hall - 147 D
 anforth Ave\, Toronto\nDoors Open: 7:00 PM ET\nShow Begins: 8:00 PM ET\nGe
 t Tickets at itsprobablynothing.com
LOCATION:The Danforth Music Hall
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/magician-chris-ramsay-its-probably-nothi
 ng-tour-with-special-comedian-guest-dave-foley-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Movie Night @ Soulpepper: Really Happy Someday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T210000
UID:blogto-235941@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/02/original_image08da2ec3-75f7-4d35-8a38-85bb368881
 13.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Soulpepper Theatre for a screening of Really Happy 
 Someday\, an indie drama set firmly in Toronto\, featuring beloved local a
 ctors.\nBefore he transitioned\, Z (Breton Lalama) was a rising musical th
 eatre star struggling with his gender identity. One year into taking testo
 sterone\, he has finally started to feel at home in his body but has lost 
 all control of his voice. At the same time\, Z’s long-term partner\, Dan
 ielle (Khadijah Roberts-Abdullah)\, feels she’s lost the person she fell
  in love with. Unable to book work with his changing voice\, Z starts bart
 ending where his new boss\, Santi\, emboldens him to fight for himself and
  his dreams. Z starts working with a singing instructor\, Shelly\, to lear
 n how to use his new voice\, and maybe even trust himself.\nFree general a
 dmission: https://www.soulpepper.ca/public-domain/whats-on/reallyhappysome
 day
LOCATION:Soulpepper Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/movie-night-soulpepper-really-happy-some
 day-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
