BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spying on America Book Launch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T190000
UID:blogto-235744@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/29/original_image6a0ce3fa-a499-4d6b-a759-9c79b1fc43
 0b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Ben McNally Books\, in partnership with Goose Lane 
 Editions\, to celebrate the launch of Spying on America\, by Bill Gaston.\
 nAbout the Book:\nOn a June morning in 2022\, Bill Gaston drives off the V
 ictoria–Port Angeles ferry in a rented Dodge Charger with his two sons. 
 Born in the USA but “Canadian through and through\,” Gaston is on a ro
 ad trip to Tabor\, Iowa\, the town founded by his great\, great\, great-gr
 andparents as the westernmost hub of the Underground Railroad.\nThe Gaston
 s’ eleven-day trip to Tabor and back takes them up and down and across a
  swathe of rural red states. Motivated equally by a curiosity to find out 
 what really makes Americans tick and the motto ya gotta stop\, the Gastons
  explore the American west\, navigate unmapped dirt roads\, eat too many F
 rench fries\, overnight in clapped-out motels\, visit a Buddhist mountain 
 monastery\, marvel at spectacular landforms\, and enjoy unlikely conversat
 ions with real Americans.\nBoth a sideways glance at contemporary American
  culture and a mordant yet tender account of the true meaning of ancestry\
 , Spying on America is an unpredictably insightful exploration of family\,
  Canada’s neighbour\, and the “American bald ego.”\nAbout the Author
 :\nBill Gaston was born in Tacoma\, Washington\, and grew up in Canada\, b
 ecoming a Canadian citizen as a teenager to avoid being drafted into the V
 ietnam War. He has lived and worked\, mostly as an itinerant scholar\, all
  across Canada\, in Nova Scotia\, New Brunswick\, Toronto\, Vancouver and\
 , finally\, Victoria. Gaston is the author of numerous books of fiction\, 
 non-fiction\, and poetry\, including The World\, winner of the Ethel Wilso
 n Prize for Fiction\; Gargoyles\, winner of the Victoria Book Prize and fi
 nalist for a Governor General’s Award\; Mount Appetite\, finalist for th
 e Giller Prize\; and the memoir Just Let Me Look at You\, finalist for the
  RBC Taylor Prize. He lives\, grows food\, and writes\, with the writer De
 de Crane\, on Gabriola Island\, in the Salish Sea.
LOCATION:Ben Mcnally Books
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/spying-on-america-book-launch-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"The Bucket Lister": Toronto's 8-Day Camping Road Trip
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T203000
UID:blogto-231436@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/02/26/original_imagefa780dbf-15cd-4788-928a-6b74c9763f
 77.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Kicking off in Toronto\, this one-off annual tour turns Ontari
 o into your very own playground for 8 days of camping\, hiking\, swimming\
 , and paddling fun. Stand tall at the edge of the world\, ride the rapids\
 , cycle a historic former railway line\, and discover sunken shipwrecks ab
 oard a glass bottom boat. You’ll never look at Ontario the same way agai
 n.\nNo guest preparation is needed\, no equipment\, not even a sleeping ba
 g/pad. Lake Fever offers travelers free transportation\, camp-cooked meals
 \, and good old fashioned campfires\, but *please be advised\, on this par
 ticular tour guests will be expected to share in cooking/dishes duties at 
 least once.* Sightseers can enjoy access to the Canadian wilderness for a 
 unique opportunity that would otherwise take a lot of planning and money t
 o arrange (not to worry\, first-timers will learn the basics of camping).\
 nToronto's own "Bucket Lister" tour visits Algonquin\, Sandbanks\, Bon Ech
 o\, and Six Mile Lake Provincial Parks\, as well as Bruce Peninsula Nation
 al Park\, Fathom Five National Marine Park\, and Elora Gorge Conservation 
 Area. Includes camping (gear and all)\, lake canoeing\, wine tasting\, man
 y breathtaking hikes\, cycling\, a glass-bottom boat tour (to shipwrecks a
 nd Flower Pot Island)\, tubing through a limestone gorge\, and a visit to 
 The Big Apple.\nCross the great Canadian road trip off your bucket list. W
 ho knows\, it may be your once-in-a-lifetime experience.\nVisit www.lakefe
 verwilderness.ca/the-bucketlister-tour for itinerary and more details.
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-bucket-lister-torontos-8-day-camping
 -road-trip-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
