 gto.com/events/2026/05/31/original_imagebdcebd38-6590-4cd3-8b30-0bd666e36c
 0d.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Learn everything you need to set up a simple\, productive and 
 easy-to-manage vegetable garden for Spring 2026!\nJoin us on Saturday\, Ju
 ne 13th\, for an in-person vegetable gardening workshop hosted by fulCircl
 e and Growing Growers. From soil stewardship to bed preparation\, planting
 \, and harvest\, you'll leave with gardening know-how and community suppor
 t!\nGrowing Growers teaches a simple\, productive gardening approach that 
 enables anyone to grow their own food. Whether you are a first-time garden
 er or a veteran grower\, you will benefit from this low-cost approach to g
 rowing delicious\, healthy food to feed you\, your family and friends. By 
 the end of this 3-hour workshop\, you will be ready to plan\, install\, pl
 ant\, tend and harvest your own growing space.\nOur workshops are ideal fo
 r:\nBeginner gardeners\nThose wanting to grow using organic\, climate-smar
 t agriculture\nThose growing in small spaces (back yards\, rooftops\, balc
 onies\, etc.)\nYou’ll receive your own starter kit to continue growing a
 t home\, including a grow bag\, soil and seedling.\nSaturday is In-Person 
 at Zawadi Farm\, 160 Downsview Park Blvd\, North York\, ON M4K 2B8.\nRain 
 or shine!\nWe also invite you to come up early or stay late to enjoy some 
 food and drinks at the new Zawadi Barn cafe.\nFree parking and accessible 
 by TTC (Downsview Park Station)
LOCATION:Zawadi Farm at Downsview Park
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/common-ground-gardening-workshop-toronto
 /
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
