BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Documentary Screening and Panel: "The Impossible Swim"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T183000
UID:blogto-235453@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/23/original_image23ed5fdd-8701-4b70-80e1-028077624a
 69.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Beach United Church for a screening of the marathon
  swim documentary The Impossible Swim (2018)\, followed by a panel with ma
 rathon swimmer and star of the documentary\, Maya Farrell\, one of the dir
 ectors of the film Larry Weinstein\, and marathon swimmer (and first openl
 y trans person to swim across Lake Ontario) Lev Goldberg.\nThis inspiring 
 film tells the story of 16-year-old swimmer Maya Farrell's quest to swim a
 cross Lake Ontario at its widest part\, with support from her family and l
 egendary marathon swimmers Marilyn Bell and Vicki Keith. This heartwarming
  film is about the courage it takes to chase big goals\, and the strength 
 and support that comes from those who believe in us.\nProceeds from this e
 vent will help pay for Lev's 55km swim across Lake Huron in August 2026\, 
 which is a fundraiser for LGBT Youthline.\n-Screening Details-\n📅 Satur
 day June 13\, 2026\n📍 Beach United Church\, 140 Wineva Ave\, Toronto\n
 ⏰ Doors Open: 4:00 PM\n⏰ Screening Start: 4:30 PM\n⏰ Post-Film Panel
  Discussion Start: 5:45 PM\n-Post-Film Panel Discussion and Audience Q&A-\
 nFollowing the screening\, join us for a live panel discussion and audienc
 e Q&A with swimmer and star of the film Maya Farrell\, director Larry Wein
 stein\, and marathon swimmer (and first trans person to swim across Lake O
 ntario) Lev Goldberg.\n-Fundraising for a Cause-\nThis screening is a fund
 raiser for Lev Goldberg's 55km swim across Lake Huron this August. Lev's s
 wim is in support of LGBT Youthline\, a peer support organization for 2SLG
 BTQ+ youth in Ontario. With his swim\, he hopes to create positive represe
 ntation of trans people in sport\, raise awareness of 2SLGBTQ+ youth menta
 l health\, and generate funds for LGBT Youthline.
LOCATION:Beach United Church (140 Wineva Ave)
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/documentary-screening-and-panel-the-impo
 ssible-swim-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Everyone Is Lying to You for Money - with Ben McKenzie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T180000
UID:blogto-235036@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/14/original_image6a0ee7b9-17aa-468c-8c74-e2ec66fa30
 fa.jpg
DESCRIPTION:“Knife-Sharp Documentary Takedown of Cryptocurrency” – V
 ariety\nIn Everyone Is Lying to You for Money\, actor and author Ben McKen
 zie turns investigator\, pulling back the curtain on the cryptocurrency in
 dustry and the culture of hype\, misinformation\, and speculation that fue
 led its explosive rise. What began as a promise of financial freedom has e
 volved into a volatile ecosystem rife with fraud and reckless gambling\, c
 arrying with it devastating consequences for everyday people.\nThrough fir
 sthand reporting\, expert interviews\, and a clear-eyed examination of maj
 or collapses and scandals\, the film traces how crypto became one of the m
 ost aggressively marketed financial products of the modern era—and how w
 arning signs were ignored\, dismissed\, or deliberately obscured. As fortu
 nes are made and lost\, Everyone Is Lying to You for Money asks a sobering
  question: who benefits from the chaos\, and who is left to clean up the d
 amage?\nAccessible\, urgent\, and often darkly ironic\, the film is both a
  cautionary tale and a call for accountability—cutting through the noise
  to expose a system built on speculation\, influence\, and belief rather t
 han truth.\nIn English and Spanish\, with English subtitles.\nJoin filmmak
 er Ben McKenzie for a special Q&A after each screening.\nBen McKenzie is t
 he only six-time Teen Choice Award nominee to have written a NYT bestselli
 ng book on economics\, as well as direct and produce a feature film on the
  subject. Easy Money and Everyone Is Lying to You for Money chronicle his 
 investigation into the murky world of cryptocurrency and fraud. Ben has st
 arred in three TV shows (Gotham\, Southland\, and The OC)\, appeared in nu
 merous films (Junebug\, Line of Duty\, The Torture Report\, and the upcomi
 ng Motor City)\, and performed on Broadway (the Tony-nominated Grand Horiz
 ons). He has written and directed multiple episodes of television. He live
 s in Brooklyn with his wife and three kids\, all of whom are tired of him 
 talking about crypto.
LOCATION:Hot Docs Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/everyone-is-lying-to-you-for-money-with-
 ben-mckenzie-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
