BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Frequency: XUKASIA
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T220000
UID:blogto-235878@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/01/original_imagee644abcc-b470-4016-8fab-129e73e6ea
 01.jpg
DESCRIPTION:June 13\n8pm\n$15-$20 adv\n$25 doors\nJoin us for Frequency 
 — a monthly live music series at Worth Gallery. Frequency spotlights BIP
 OC musicians of varying genres through intimate\, stripped-back shows. Cel
 ebrating sound\, connection\, and creative expression in Toronto's vibrant
  music scene. Find your new favorite musician in your new favorite gallery
 .\nThis edition of Frequency features XUKASIA\, resident noisy music wallf
 lower. She'll be accompanied by experimental-techno producer/DJ Plastic He
 art Surgery.\nXUKASIA is a rapper and producer from Toronto\, creating exp
 erimental abstract soundscapes within the genres of hip-hop\, hardcore ele
 ctronic\, industrial\, punk\, ambient\, breakcore and synthwave house musi
 c. She's released two albums: "XONIKA!" and "XEONFLUXX!"\nHer lyrics are o
 ften raw and personal\, detailing her experiences with topics such as gend
 er identity\, mental health issues\, and manifesting positive energy. She 
 makes all her beats using FL Studio and an AKAI MPK midi controller. XUKAS
 IA is also a show organizer\, putting on multiple series of showcases like
  AFRONOIZE (Black queer showcase\, all genres) and ARMAGEDDON (queer exper
 imental showcase).\nLocated in the lower gallery — down a flight of stai
 rs.\nFor any other accessibility questions\, please feel free to reach out
  to us.
LOCATION:Worth Gallery
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/frequency-xukasia-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gay AF Comedy Pride-Stravaganza!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T163000
UID:blogto-234519@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/02/original_imagee1cc5ad6-1cdf-4efa-8f62-17cb26a8e9
 09.jpg
DESCRIPTION:GAY AF COMEDY PRIDE-STRAVAGANZA is back at Campbell House Muse
 um for its 5th year! Come join the funny for some big Queer laughs! An Off
 icial Pride Toronto Major Cultural Event!\nGay AF Comedy Pride-Stravaganza
  is taking over the stunning Campbell House Museum gardens for an All-Star
  Outdoor Queer Comedy event\, with headliner and Queer comedy treasure MAR
 THA CHAVES! Now in our 5th year of fantastic fierce fun!\nKnown for servin
 g fabulous comic lineups that “will make your jaw drop” (She Does The 
 City)\, Gay AF is Toronto’s premiere place for A-List headliners and a Q
 ueer cornucopia of supporting acts. Enjoy free sampling by our exclusive d
 rinks sponsor Cottage Springs Beverage Co. and experience some of Canada
 ’s top Queer comedic talent in a wonderful outdoor setting.\nHeadliner M
 ARTHA CHAVES (Canadian Comedy Award winner\, credits include JFL\, Winnipe
 g Festival\, The Debaters\, Because News)\nFeaturing Gay AF faves BEE BERT
 RAND\, NILE SEGUIN\, TAMARA APPLETON & MIKAEL MELO!\nHosted by Canadian Co
 medy Award winner ROBERT WATSON\n“Queer and Hilarious\, with BDE” – 
 My Gay Toronto\n“a joyful event with a little something for everyone” 
 – Parton & Pearl\n“featuring top-notch queer comedians who represent t
 he many intersections of the LGBTQ2S+ community.” – IN Magazine\nSatur
 day June 13. Gates 2pm / Show 3pm. The Campbell House Museum Outdoor Garde
 ns. 160 Queen Street West (Near Osgoode Subway Station). Tickets $30.\nCom
 e Join The Funny this Pride!\nACCESSIBILITY\nWhile the outdoor gardens are
  uneven in places they are accessible for mobility devices. Washrooms are 
 located inside the museum down a flight of stairs.
LOCATION:Campbell House Museum
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/gay-af-comedy-pride-stravaganza-toronto-
 5/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Glad Day Lit's Pride Month Artist Market - June 13
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T180000
UID:blogto-235707@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/28/original_imagede9f24f3-06c4-4f02-8cae-df06be76e4
 b0.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A Saturday full of incredible artists! Support queer & trans a
 rt! FREE entry - get something special for yourself or someone you love.\n
 One of many Pride Month artist markets at Glad Day Lit! Over 60 vendors be
 tween June 6th & 13th! RSVP for the Eventbrite for the 6th while you're he
 re and claim your chance to win a $25 credit to the market!\nThis is FREE 
 to attend but if you RSVP you get entered into a draw to get $25 to spend 
 at the market! Name will be drawn the night before the event. One entry pe
 r person.\nVendors:\n(For more vendor info check our instagram @gladdayboo
 kshop!)\nCeramics AF\nsallarts\nGRRRL Spells\nHazie Days\nA. Moritsugu Art
 \nRad Habits\nruuari\nlynx.frog\nsaf.bug\nPavić Studios\nSuexine\nKavi\nV
 ethereal\nMonster Cliche\nJuno's Corner\nspekterjester\nI.Z.A. Studios\nra
 dlo studio\nAnam Creations\nLola\nKeyana Allen (sykeart)\nStitch Witch Cra
 fters\nStable Hands\nMargh\nPhynn Saunders\nShura K\ndairysam\nKeet\nNiamh
  Rose\nNic ter Horst\nCozy By Aliana\nThe entrance\, washroom and space ar
 e wheelchair accessible.\nMOBILITY DEVICE ACCESSIBILITY : IMPORTANT ALTERN
 ATIVE because of snow(this is a note for people in wheelchairs\, scooter\,
  with a walker or folks who cannot do more than 2 stairs)\nWhile our front
  door and the inside of the space is accessible\, some environmental facto
 rs (like snow) can impact the path to the front door through the park. So 
 here is the accessible alternative:\nYou can access our front door by goin
 g through the condo next door.\nOPTION #1: 21 Abell St - Get dropped off o
 r picked up at 21 Abell and enter the condo from the east side. Go through
  the lobby and then out the north (main) door\, you are then at Glad Day.\
 nOPTION #2: Get dropped off at the parking garage behind 47 Abell / 16 Lis
 gar. Enter the condo from the south side\, which is a covered driveway beh
 ind the condo. You enter from the south\, you walk through the lobby and t
 hen out the north (main) door\, you are then at Glad Day. This one can be 
 tricky so the 21 Abell option is often more reliable.
LOCATION:Glad Day Lit
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/glad-day-lits-pride-month-artist-market-
 june-13-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
