 0b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The Hope Gala and Awards Ceremony\, celebrating its 21st year\
 , is a cornerstone event for SCAGO. The gala raises essential funds to sup
 port initiatives for patients and families affected by sickle cell disease
  (SCD) and honours individuals who have made significant contributions to 
 SCD awareness\, research\, and treatment in Canada. Past galas have welcom
 ed over 500 notable guests\, including politicians\, healthcare profession
 als\, and community leaders.\nEvent Details\nDate: Saturday\, June 13\, 20
 26\nTime: Doors open at 5:30 PM EST | Program runs from 6:30 PM to 9:30 PM
 \nLocation: Salons B and C\, Renaissance by the Creek\n3045B Southcreek Rd
  Unit 58\, Mississauga\, ON\, L4X 2X7\nTicket Information:\nIndividual tic
 kets are available for $150 CAD\, and tables of eight are available for $1
 \,150 CAD. Tickets can be purchased online.\nWe invite you to join us for 
 the evening. Your coverage would greatly enhance awareness and support for
  individuals and families affected by SCD.
LOCATION:Renaissance by the Creek
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/hope-gala-and-awards-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Become a Volunteer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T150000
UID:blogto-233999@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/22/original_image5d92d6f8-5a13-414f-9712-df3b45716a
 b7.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning more about volunteering opportunities i
 n Toronto?\nThis session is intended for the volunteer seekers who are new
  to volunteering\, or in need to understand the process of formal voluntee
 ring. Join us to learn how and where to search for opportunities that best
  match your interests and what to expect after you apply for a volunteer r
 ole.\nThis session caters to all demographics.\nPresented by Volunteer Tor
 onto.
LOCATION:Toronto Public Library - Richview Branch
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/how-to-become-a-volunteer-toronto/
