BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:I Am Divine - with Michelle Mama
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T210000
UID:blogto-235039@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/14/original_imagec7d031fb-6f4b-4e52-bb26-45c756eb81
 e6.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Having just joined us at Hot Docs Festival for the world premi
 ere of her new film Antidiva: The Carole Pope Confessions\, filmmaker Mich
 elle Mama is back to present a film about another legendary queer icon—o
 ne with a curious Carole connection.\n“Divine is a one-of-one star in ou
 r queer constellation. She came out of the same tough post-war industrial 
 Baltimore world as John Waters and together they created a collection of w
 ild\, raunchy and hilarious series of films like Pink Flamingos and Female
  Trouble that are still too vile and disgusting for polite company. A dire
 ctor and his muse were never more sympatico than these two rebellious crea
 tures. I thought the only connection between Toronto and Divine was that t
 he 2007 remake of Hairspray - the original being the most commercial of al
 l the Waters films and\, tragically Divine’s last - was shot here. But a
 s I was working on Antidiva: The Carole Pope Confessions\, I learned that 
 Divine and Rough Trade did a one-night-only musical called Restless Underw
 ear on December 19th\, 1977\, that Carole describes as “titillating and 
 stupid. In short it was everything we aspired to.” This Carole connectio
 n was more than enough for me to seal the deal on selecting I Am Divine as
  my queer doc pick for Hot Docs' Pride Projected this year.The heightened 
 absurdity of her comedy and performances\, and her relentless grit and hea
 rtbreaking sweetness make Divine one of the most beloved and important art
 ists and agitators of the 20th century.” – Michelle Mama on Divine and
  I Am Divine\nI Am Divine is the story of Divine\, aka Harris Glenn Milste
 ad\, from his humble beginnings as an overweight\, teased Baltimore youth 
 to internationally recognized drag superstar through his collaboration wit
 h filmmaker John Waters. Spitting in the face of the status quos of body i
 mage\, gender identity\, sexuality\, and preconceived notions of beauty\, 
 Divine was the ultimate outsider turned underground royalty. With a comple
 tely committed in-your-face style\, he blurred the line between performer 
 and personality\, and revolutionized pop culture. I Am Divine is a definit
 ive biographical portrait that charts the legendary icon’s rise to infam
 y and emotional complexities.\nI Am Divine will be presented with a live i
 ntroduction from Michelle Mama.\nMichelle Mama is an award-winning\, five-
 time Canadian Screen Award nominee who has been producing and directing in
  the factual and doc space for over two decades. Her latest film\, Antidiv
 a: The Carole Pope Confessions\, was selected as the Opening Night Film fo
 r the 2026 Hot Docs Festival\, where it received its world premiere and pl
 aced #6 in the 2026 Top 20 Audience Favourites.
LOCATION:Hot Docs Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/i-am-divine-with-michelle-mama-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
