BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Island Eats Food and Travel Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T220000
UID:blogto-234900@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/11/original_image95f64032-d5e6-43ab-bcbf-549269e813
 98.jpg
DESCRIPTION:🌴 Toronto\, It's Time to Vibe Out — Island Eats Is BACK\n
 Forget booking a flight. This June\, the Caribbean comes straight to Toron
 to — free of charge.\nIsland Eats Food & Travel Festival returns to Mel 
 Lastman Square on Saturday\, June 13 (1 PM – 10 PM) and Sunday\, June 14
  (1 PM – 8 PM).\n🔥 Feel It In Your Chest\nJerk chicken\, doubles\, pe
 pper pot\, tropical mocktails and the "Breeze and Brews" bar serving cockt
 ails\, mocktails and Caribbean beer. Bold flavours\, pulsing rhythms and c
 ultural displays that hit different.\n"When you're here\, you feel it in y
 our chest — the music\, the food the laughter. That's generations of cul
 ture\, joy and resilience showing up in one place." -Petronilla Marchan\, 
 Festival Manager\n🎤 Non-Stop Entertainment\n🥁 Live steelpan with Rhy
 thm & Pan on D' Greens\n🎧 DJs spinning soca\, calypso\, reggae and danc
 ehall all day\n🎭 Moko jumbies and carnival characters in full costume\n
 💃 FREE drop-in dance classes - soca wining\, dancehall and salsa\, plus
  a Sunday Community Dance Showcase\n⚡ Pop-up performances and cultural s
 howcases throughout the weekend\n👨‍🍳 Junior Chef Competition ft. G
 race Foods Canada\nYoung chefs take the stage in this sponsored cooking co
 mpetition judged by celebrated Caribbean chefs. The winner takes home a ca
 sh prize and a featured spot in the Island Eats digital cookbook.\n🏆 Th
 e Golden Roti Challenge\nThink you can handle a festival-sized curry roti?
  The winner of this crowd-favourite eating competition walks away with tic
 kets to their favourite island destination!\n🎨 Caribbean Craft Market &
  Artist Village\nOver 30 Black and Caribbean artists\, designers and maker
 s selling original prints\, jewellery\, ceramics\, hot sauces and one-of-a
 -kind pieces. Shop small\, shop Caribbean.\n🌅 Sunset Golden Hour — Sa
 turday 8 PM–10 PM\nThe square transforms into an open-air party with spe
 cial lighting\, a curated DJ set and a Caribbean cocktail tasting experien
 ce featuring signature drinks from six island nations.\n✈️ One Taste I
 s Never Enough\nThe tourism booths from Jamaica\, Barbados\, Trinidad & To
 bago\, Antigua & Barbuda\, Saint Lucia\, and Grenada aren't just there to 
 hand out brochures — they're there to remind you that what you're tastin
 g and hearing this weekend is just a preview. The real thing - the ocean\,
  the air\, the people\, the food fresh from the source - is waiting for yo
 u. Let the festival light the spark\, and let them help you fan the flame.
 \n💛 Give Back While You Celebrate\nIsland Eats is a Caribbean Scholarsh
 ip Foundation (CSF) fundraiser\, supporting scholarships\, mentorship\, an
 d the arts across the Caribbean diaspora. Every bite counts.\n📍 The Det
 ails\n📅 Sat\, June 13 — 1 PM to 10 PM · Sun\, June 14 — 1 PM to 8 
 PM\n📍 Mel Lastman Square\, Toronto · 💸 FREE admission\nGrab your cr
 ew\, show up hungry\, and leave with a serious case of island fever — an
 d maybe a one-way search open on your phone. 🌊🥭🎶
LOCATION:Mel Lastman Square
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/island-eats-food-and-travel-festival-tor
 onto-3/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
