 0e.jpg
DESCRIPTION:From flying boats and wartime pilots to commuter flights skimm
 ing the waterfront\, explore the history of Billy Bishop Toronto City Airp
 ort and its transformation from a former military training base to a gatew
 ay connecting Toronto to the world. This waterfront walk traces the airpor
 t’s remarkable evolution through stories of aviation pioneers\, Norwegia
 n airmen\, island amusement parks\, and the communities shaped by the harb
 our’s constant movement and change. Discover how this small island airpo
 rt became a gateway for millions—and how global events\, innovation\, an
 d local debates transformed Toronto’s shoreline along the way.
LOCATION:Southwest corner of Queens Quay West and Eireann Quay
