 to’s oldest industrial crossroads—now a rapidly changing urban communi
 ty.\nOnce a bustling industrial crossroads\, the Canary District has trans
 formed into a growing urban village shaped by movement and migration. On t
 his walk\, uncover stories of Irish immigrants\, railway workers\, factori
 es\, freight yards\, and working-class life woven into the neighbourhood
 ’s streets and buildings. We’ll explore the layers of change tied to i
 ts history as a shipping hub and working-class enclave\, its transformatio
 n during the 2015 Pan Am Games\, and the community taking shape today.
