 db.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Hello\,\nWe are hosting networking and career elevation event 
 for newcomers- Find Your Niche: Newcomer Professionals Career Forum- a one
  day networking and career development event created specifically for skil
 led newcomer professionals looking to reconnect with meaningful career pat
 hways and to build social capital in Canada.\nThis event is especially rel
 evant for internationally trained professionals in healthcare\, tech\, eng
 ineering\, entrepreneurship\, consulting\, sectors who are looking to expa
 nd their networks\, gain industry insight\, and access opportunities align
 ed with their education and experience. Participants will have access to t
 ailored résumé feedback\, career insights\, and opportunities to connect
  directly with professionals and organizations that understand newcomer ca
 reer pathways.\nThis is going to be the full schedule of the day event:\nA
 genda\n09:30 AM - 10:00 AM\nRegistration\nSign-in\, plan your day\, and en
 joy light refreshments (coffee\, tea\, and snacks) provided by SCCC.\n10:0
 0 AM - 04:00 PM\nInformation Fair\n11:00 AM - 11:15 AM\nWelcome and Openin
 g Remarks\n11:15 AM - 11:45 AM\nKeynote Speaker\n12:00 PM - 01:00 PM\nSimu
 ltaneous Programming (3 Options)\nJoin one of our three programming option
 s\; 1. Career Coaching Session\, hosted by the Diversity Institute at Toro
 nto Metropolitan University. Spots are limited- Day-of registration is req
 uired. 2. Panel Discussion: Pivoting- Moving into a New Career as an Exper
 ienced Professional 3. Networking & Social Capital Skills Workshop\n01:30 
 PM - 02:30 PM\nLunch Hour\nLunch Vendor Options onsite include SCCC progra
 m alumni entrepreneurs with items $10 and under. Vegetarian\, GF\, and Hal
 al options will be available. Market 707 vendors are also onsite. A free l
 unch will not be provided.\n02:00 PM - 03:00 PM\nSimultaneous Programming 
 (3 options)\n1. Career Coaching (Session #2)\, hosted by the Diversity Ins
 titute at Toronto Metropolitan University. Spots are limited-day-of regist
 ration is required. 2. LinkedIn Headshots Booth - Spots are limited- Day-o
 f registration is required. 3. Networking Session- AI-enabled networking. 
 Spots are limited- Sign-up prior to June 20 registration required.\n03:00 
 PM - 04:00 PM\nNetworking and Coffee\nCome together in our main event area
  to close out the day and make final connections with other attendees and 
 our exhibitors. Coffee and light refreshments will be provided.\nThe event
  is free to attend and open to newcomers\, international professionals\, a
 nd emerging leaders interested in career growth and community connection.\
 nMore details and free registration available on the Eventbrite page. Link
  is shared here and down below as well https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/find-yo
 ur-niche-newcomer-career-forum-tickets-1987003986412?aff=oddtdtcreator\nTh
 ank you so much for your support
