BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paddles for Progress
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T153000
UID:blogto-234418@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/29/original_image53340e2c-12d1-4a10-8717-d1b7354d69
 69.jpg
DESCRIPTION:CAMH Engage’s Paddles for Progress returns for its third yea
 r on Saturday\, June 20\, and this one is set to be the biggest yet.\nJoin
  us at the Fairgrounds Racket Club in Leaside for a full day of play\, now
  featuring both Pickleball and Padel tournaments.\nIn support of the CAMH 
 Foundation\, the event brings together sport\, community\, and a shared co
 mmitment to mental health. Throughout the day\, guests can expect bites fr
 om local vendors and a silent auction. After the tournaments wrap\, the cr
 owd continues to The Porch Toronto for a social event that brings players\
 , supporters\, and volunteers together. Access to the social is available 
 as an add-on ticket.\nSince launching in 2024\, Paddles for Progress has r
 aised over $111K for CAMH\, with 100% of proceeds donated directly to supp
 ort mental health research and care. This year\, the focus is on building 
 on that momentum and extending the impact even further.\nWhether you’re 
 playing\, cheering\, or just coming for the atmosphere\, it’s a great wa
 y to spend a Saturday while supporting better access to mental health care
 .\nPickleball and Padel Tournament\nLocation: Fairgrounds Public Racket Cl
 ub\n849 Eglinton Ave E\, East York\, ON M4G 2L5\nTime: 9:30-3:30pm\nSporty
  Social Event\nLocation: The Porch Toronto\n250 Adelaide St W\, Toronto ON
  M5H 1X6\nTime: 7pm - late
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/paddles-for-progress-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Parade: Queer Acts of Love & Resistance - FREE Pride Documentary S
 creening
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T164500
UID:blogto-234784@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/07/original_image47a04189-bc94-426e-a78b-d47c9da2e5
 7f.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Parade: Queer Acts of Love & Resistance captures pivotal momen
 ts that sparked Canada’s 2SLGBTQI+ movement\, honouring the activists an
 d elders whose resistance led to the rights we have today.\nThrough rarely
  seen archival footage and first-person accounts\, audiences are brought t
 o the frontlines of the struggle. From police raids to early drag shows\, 
 community organizing to the House of Commons—the complex history of the 
 country’s diverse communities is brought to life. Key milestones illustr
 ate the power of taking it into the streets and underscore how easily the 
 rights we’ve fought for can be revoked\, making the documentary essentia
 l viewing for all Canadians.\nUnflinching\, bold\, enraging\, hopeful\; Pa
 rade is a vital new chapter in the queer canon.\nThis screening is present
 ed in collaboration with the National Film Board of Canada\, which is Cana
 da’s only public producer and distributor of Canadian films and series.
LOCATION:Palmerston Library
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/parade-queer-acts-of-love-resistance-fre
 e-pride-documentary-screening-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
