BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TIME AND TRANSFORMATION
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T220000
UID:blogto-231314@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/02/23/original_imageb54a9207-96fa-467a-b2ed-b372d7c7fe
 a9.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Hungarian composer Erno Dohnanyi’s Symphonic Minutes is divi
 ded into five movements\, each only one or two minutes in length. Each mov
 ement retains a typically classical form\, including a rhapsody\, a scherz
 o\, a theme and variations\, as well as a rondo. Michael Berkovsky and Cor
 al Solomon then perform Poulenc’s Concerto for two pianos and orchestra.
  Inspired by Mozart and Balinese gamelan\, the work features lively rhythm
 s\, graceful melodies\, and playful dialogue between the two pianos and or
 chestra\, blending wit\, lyricism\, and brilliance. Finnish composer Jean 
 Sibelius structured his Symphony no. 2 from a rising three-note motif out 
 of which all other themes are generated—a compositional practice Arnold 
 Schoenberg described as “developing variation.” The first movement als
 o bears a relationship to Richard Strauss’ famous tone poem\, Tod und Ve
 rklärung: both have the main theme emerge in full only at the end\, rathe
 r than the beginning.\nKristian Alexander | conductor\nMichael Berkovsky 
 – Coral Solomon | piano duo\nDaniel Vnukowski | host\n7:10 p.m. Prélude
 : pre-concert recital.\n7:20 p.m. Pre-concert talk.\nIntermission discussi
 on and Q&A with Michael Berkovsky\, Coral Solomon and Daniel Vnukowski.
LOCATION:Meridian Arts Centre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/time-and-transformation-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
