BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:THE 3rd Space No. 1 : Opera Arias of Identity\, War\, Exile\, Home
 land and Diaspora
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T160000
UID:blogto-235394@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/22/original_imageb6104e2e-0042-4958-b7e2-0720fa7f63
 c5.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Cultureland Opera Collective proudly presents THE 3rd Space No
 . 1: Opera Arias of Identity\, War\, Exile\, Homeland and Diaspora — a u
 nique concert experience that bridges music\, history\, storytelling\, and
  cultural reflection through the powerful world of opera.\nAt the heart of
  this program lies the idea of the “third space” — an invisible emot
 ional and psychological space many people carry within themselves between 
 homeland and new land\, memory and reality\, belonging and displacement. S
 haped by migration\, war\, longing\, love\, loss\, and transformation\, th
 is space speaks deeply to contemporary human experience.\nThrough a curate
 d selection of opera arias and art songs spanning different historical per
 iods\, audiences are invited on a journey through some of opera’s most p
 rofound voices of exile\, abandonment\, identity\, displacement\, and resi
 lience. The program explores how composers across history transformed huma
 n struggle\, political upheaval\, and emotional conflict into music that c
 ontinues to resonate powerfully today.\nMore than a traditional concert\, 
 THE 3rd Space offers audiences a guided historical and emotional explorati
 on. Alongside live performances\, the program includes curated commentary 
 and contextual storytelling that illuminate the historical\, political\, a
 nd human realities behind these iconic works\, revealing opera not as a di
 stant art form of the past\, but as a living reflection of collective huma
 n experience.\nFounded by Iranian-Canadian composer and curator Dr. Afarin
  Mansouri\, Cultureland Opera Collective is dedicated to building bridges 
 between cultures through contemporary opera\, intercultural performance\, 
 and educational initiatives that connect diverse communities to the operat
 ic art form.\nTHE 3rd Space is the first program in an ongoing concert ser
 ies exploring opera through themes of identity\, migration\, humanity\, me
 mory\, and social transformation.
LOCATION:Nancy & Ed Jackman Performance Centre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-3rd-space-no-1-opera-arias-of-identi
 ty-war-exile-homeland-and-diaspora-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
