ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/13/original_imagecb29d3b2-0c9f-490e-ab46-8846ae978a
 a1.jpg
DESCRIPTION:AiRTIFICIAL VISIONS is an immersive exhibition in Toronto that
  explores the intersection of art\, artificial intelligence\, and human id
 entity. Presented by Rogers at Illuminarium Toronto\, as part of the Lavaz
 za IncluCity Festival by ICFF\, the exhibition brings together leading int
 ernational AI artists to examine the human figure in the digital age. Thro
 ugh large-scale visuals\, immersive environments\, and poetic storytelling
 \, it invites audiences to reflect on how technology is transforming creat
 ivity and our perception of ourselves. Developed in collaboration with Tor
 onto Metropolitan University\, the program also features conversations and
  panels that explore the evolving relationship between art\, AI\, and huma
 n expression.
LOCATION:ILLUMINARIUM TORONTO\, DISTILLERY DISTRICT
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/airtificial-visions-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
