BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Taste of the Junction 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T190000
UID:blogto-233779@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/17/original_imagedc7b34f8-26af-4bd3-a19f-c1d18fab77
 70.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Toronto’s west end is coming alive this summer! The Junction
  BIA invites residents and visitors to experience Taste of the Junction 20
 26\, a one-day outdoor market and cultural celebration on Saturday\, June 
 27\, from 11:00 a.m. to 7:00 p.m. in the Green P parking lot at 385 Pacifi
 c Avenue\, just south of Dundas Street West. The event is expected to draw
  thousands for a day of local food\, culture\, creativity\, and neighbourh
 ood discovery—capturing Toronto’s spirit as The World in a City.\nVisi
 tors can explore 50+ vendor booths\, shop unique creations from local make
 rs\, enjoy bites and drinks from neighbourhood favourites\, and dive into 
 pop-up experiences for all ages. The day will be energized by DJ programmi
 ng\, a vibrant market atmosphere\, and a family-friendly Play Zone hosted 
 within the Darren’s No Frills footprint.\nA signature feature of this ye
 ar’s event is Passageways\, five immersive\, walk-in cultural installati
 ons created by local artists. Housed in 10 x 10-ft tents\, each installati
 on transforms a small footprint into a richly layered\, photo-worthy cultu
 ral environment filled with colour\, texture\, storytelling\, and interact
 ive elements. The Passageways celebrate five of the Junction’s largest c
 ultural communities: British\, Black\, South Asian\, Chinese\, and Portugu
 ese\, incorporating tactile features and audio guides via QR code for a la
 yered\, multi-sensory experience.\nVisitors are also encouraged to explore
  the neighbourhood beyond the event site by discovering the Junction’s 1
 1 permanent animated augmented reality murals using the free Artivive app.
  As Toronto’s only year-round AR Destination\, the Junction offers self-
 guided AR Mural Tour maps online and at the Taste of the Junction booth\, 
 making it easy to explore\, discover\, and interact with public art throug
 hout the neighbourhood.
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/taste-of-the-junction-2026-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Adjuster
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T170000
UID:blogto-233547@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/13/original_image403a06ac-28f0-4805-a79c-9a265b847e
 46.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Noah Render (Elias Koteas) is an insurance claims adjuster who
  attends to his clients’ every need—including their sexual ones. His w
 ife\, Hera (Arsinée Khanjian)\, is a government censor who spends her day
 s and nights obsessively watching pornography for both work and pleasure. 
 When they become involved with Bubba (Maury Chaykin) and Mimi (Gabrielle R
 ose)\, a wealthy couple with a taste for kinky role-playing\, the Renders
 ’ lives are turned upside down in this surreal puzzle from Atom Egoyan. 
 Criterion Collection\nPair with Curious Minds // Toronto: Cinema City - wi
 th Eric Veillette - Week 3: Classified by the Ontario Board of Censors (Sa
 turday\, June 20).
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-adjuster-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
