BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Canada Day 2026 at the THM
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T170000
UID:blogto-235623@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/27/original_imagea2e80448-fcc1-4dc6-873d-8197150ab6
 ea.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Use comp code CANADA2026 at checkout on July 1 to take advanta
 ge of complimentary tickets for this special day at the Museum.\nSpend thi
 s Canada Day with the Toronto Holocaust Museum (THM) and Jewish Immigrant 
 Aid Services (JIAS)\, finding inspiration in the enduring strength of refu
 gees and the stories of Holocaust survivors and descendants who help shape
  the fabric of Canadian society.\nExplore experiences of survival\, immigr
 ation\, and rebuilding throughout the galleries. Participate in artmaking 
 activities inspired by Silhouettes of Survival\, a special installation by
  artist Rosette Sund that explores the experiences of people who came to C
 anada after the devastation of the Second World War.\nEngage with the exhi
 bition\, Sponsorship Stories\, on view in the Ekstein Family Learning Lab.
  JIAS created this exhibition to celebrate 10 years of life-changing work 
 of sponsoring refugees\, helping them to resettle and find community here.
  Through personal stories of courage\, commitment\, and community\, the ex
 hibition invites visitors to reflect on what these experiences reveal abou
 t Canada today.\nThis program is recommended for ages 12 and up.\nThis pro
 gram is supported by UJA’s Kultura Collective project grant. The Silho
 uettes of Survival installation is presented in partnership with Jewish Im
 migrant Aid Services and the Ontario Jewish Archives Blankenstein Family H
 eritage Centre.
LOCATION:Toronto Holocaust Museum
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/canada-day-2026-at-the-thm-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
