 gto.com/events/2026/01/06/original_image55e23622-b7d9-46b1-889d-03c440fc43
 c5.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Experience a week of a global gathering of harpists\, educator
 s\, and music lovers celebrating the harp’s timeless beauty and boundles
 s future.\nThe Toronto International Harp Festival (iHarpFest) brings the 
 world’s most distinguished harpists together at two of Toronto’s most 
 inspiring venues — the Aga Khan Museum and The Ismaili Centre — for a 
 celebration of culture\, creativity\, and connection.\nFrom Queen Victoria
  to Broadway settings\, from ancient strings to contemporary sounds\, iHar
 pFest 2026 will transform Toronto into the most diverse international stag
 e for the harp — the world’s most ethereal instrument.\nJuly 11 Saturd
 ay Location: Ismaili Center Toronto - Social Hall\n50 Harps. One Sound. To
 ronto Voices Unite.\nTier Ticket - Rear: $60\nTier Ticket -  Centre: $65\n
 Harp Concerto Night with National Broadcast Orchestra\nTier Ticket - Rear:
  $75\nTier Ticket - Centre:  $85\nJuly 12 Sunday Location: Aga Khan Museum
  - Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\nHarpist to Her Majesty. A Victorian
  Tribute.\nTier Ticket - Balcony: $65\nTier Ticket - Orchestra: $75\nHarp 
 Meets Theatre: "Woman on a Ledge"\nTier Ticket - Balcony: $70\nTier Ticket
  - Orchestra: $80
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-international-harp-festival-toro
 nto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
