 gto.com/events/2026/06/02/original_imaged252eb0a-73ff-4686-bad6-504fc13eb8
 9b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Under the open sky of Toronto’s iconic High Park\, Shakespea
 re’s beloved romantic comedy comes to life. When Viola is shipwrecked an
 d disguises herself as a man\, she sets off a whirlwind of mistaken identi
 ties\, mischievous schemes\, and tangled romances.\nAs disguises unravel a
 nd hearts collide\, Twelfth Night delivers laughter\, music\, and the joyf
 ul chaos of love. Pack a picnic\, gather your friends\, and enjoy a summer
  night of theatre under the stars.
LOCATION:High Park Amphitheatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/twelfth-night-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Canadian Photography Conference 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T140000
UID:blogto-235607@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/27/original_imagea2186a75-f1a4-4f08-bd4c-aebc6d36e2
 e5.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Come experience how our shared love of photography can connect
 \, inspire\, and equip us to share our nation's stories at the Canadian Ph
 otography Conference 2026!\nJoin us July 13-16\, 2026\, in where the Footh
 ills Camera Club and the Canadian Association for Photographic Art are hos
 ting an unforgettable gathering of creativity\, artistry\, and community.\
 nThe schedule features speakers with diverse genres\, including a high-oct
 ane look at capturing split-second action from Olympian-turned-photographe
 r Kelly VanderBeek\, a deep dive into powerful documentary storytelling wi
 th Nadya Kwandibens\, and practical insights on using wildlife images for 
 activism with premier conservation photographer John E. Marriott. From Ric
 hard Martin’s abstract fine-art techniques and Monika Deviat’s mesmeri
 zing night sky masterpieces to Craig Hilts’ adrenaline-fueled prairie st
 orm chasing\, the event is packed with dynamic presentations\, trade shows
 \, and hands-on excursions designed to inspire creators of all skill level
 s.\nAttend Online\nFor the first time ever\, the conference is going hybri
 d!  You can still join virtually with live-stream access and 12 months of 
 on-demand recordings.\nThe Live-Stream option also allows real time transl
 ation through YouTube Live and Google Translate for attendees whose primar
 y language is not English.
LOCATION:Virtual Event
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/canadian-photography-conference-2026-tor
 onto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
