 7c.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Experience the Ultimate Celebration of African & Caribbean Cul
 ture!\nJoin us for the 14th annual  Afro-Carib Fest\, an award-winning\, F
 REE weekend festival that celebrates the vibrant Afro-Caribbean culture th
 rough live music\, dance\, food\, and art!\n📅   Date: August 22nd & 23r
 d\, 2026\n⏰  Time: 12 PM – 9 PM\n📍     Location: Thomson Memorial P
 ark\, Scarborough\n✨ What to Expect:\n🎶 Live Performances – Enjoy e
 lectrifying shows from 120+ local & international artists\n🥘 New Taste 
 of Afro-Carib Fest food competition\n🛍️ Vendor Marketplace – Shop u
 nique cultural treasures\,  gifts\, arts and crafts\, from local businesse
 s\n🍲 Food Zone – Indulge in mouth-watering African & Caribbean delica
 cies\n💃  Dance Competitions – Show off your dance moves & win cash pr
 izes\n🥁  Drum & Dance Workshops – Learn from the best and engage with
  our local artists\n🎧 DJ Sound Clash – Non-stop beats from our top DJ
 s\n🎭 Cultural Parade – A vibrant showcase of heritage & traditions! C
 ome with your cultural flags\n🎟️ Raffle Draws – Win exciting prizes
  including hotel stays\, Toronto attractions and more!\n👨‍👩‍👧
 ‍👦 Kids & Family Zone – Face painting\, bouncy castle and fun activ
 ities for all ages\nWhether you're coming for the high-energy performances
 \, the delicious food\, or the cultural experience\, there's something for
  everyone at Afro-Carib Fest!\n🔥 Don't miss out on this unforgettable c
 elebration! Mark your calendar and invite your friends & family.\nFor more
  details\, visit https://afrocaribfestival.com or follow us on https://www
 .instagram.com/afrocaribfest/\nSee you there! 🎊🌍🎶
