BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Guided Walk: Streets and Place Names
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260823T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260823T150000
UID:blogto-234435@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/30/original_imagedf96b311-57d7-445a-aea7-8212896364
 96.jpg
DESCRIPTION:What’s in a street name?\nRecent conversations about street 
 and place names — and who or what they commemorate — have highlighted 
 how these everyday markers quietly shape our sense of identity\, belonging
 \, and exclusion. The names we pass by without a second thought can tell p
 owerful stories about a neighbourhood’s past\, its values\, and whose hi
 stories are centred.\nThis guided walk\, led by artist and scholar Andrew 
 Lochhead\, invites you to see the city differently. Thinking of street nam
 es as the most visible “texts” of a city\, we’ll explore the streets
  surrounding the Bata Shoe Museum and uncover the meanings behind their na
 mes. Together\, we’ll consider what these names reveal about the Annex n
 eighbourhood\, its histories\, and its wider connections.\nAfter the walk\
 , we’ll gather back inside the museum for a collaborative discussion\, s
 haring what we “read” along the way and reflecting on how public namin
 g shapes the stories our city tells.\nThe walk will take up to two hours. 
 Please wear comfortable shoes.
LOCATION:Bata Shoe Museum
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/guided-walk-streets-and-place-names-toro
 nto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Heart World Conference 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260823T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260824T060000
UID:blogto-229080@blogto.com
DESCRIPTION:Heart World Conference 2026 (HWC 2026)\nAugust 23–25\, 2026 
 | Dubai\, UAE & Virtual\nPrecision Global Conferences warmly invites you t
 o the Heart World Conference (HWC 2026)\, scheduled to take place from Aug
 ust 23 to 25\, 2026\, in Dubai\, UAE\, with a comprehensive hybrid format 
 enabling both in-person and virtual participation.\nThis premier internati
 onal forum will bring together cardiologists\, cardiac surgeons\, interven
 tional specialists\, researchers\, nurses\, allied healthcare professional
 s\, public health experts\, and healthcare innovators committed to advanci
 ng cardiovascular science and improving heart health outcomes worldwide.\n
 Conference Theme\n"Heart Health for All: Advancing Global Strategies in Ca
 rdiology" Cardiovascular diseases remain the leading cause of mortality gl
 obally\, with rising burdens from coronary artery disease\, heart failure\
 , arrhythmias\, hypertension\, and cardiometabolic disorders. Coupled with
  disparities in access to care and rapidly evolving technologies\, the nee
 d for collaborative\, evidence-based\, and patient-centered cardiovascular
  solutions has never been more urgent. HWC 2026 provides a timely and esse
 ntial platform to address cardiovascular health across the continuum—fro
 m fundamental research and advanced diagnostics to innovative therapeutics
 \, preventive cardiology\, digital health\, and policy implementation.\n
 🔗 Quick Links\n🔗 More Information:\nhttps://www.heartconferences.pre
 cisionglobalcon.com/\n🔗 Submit Abstracts:\nhttps://www.heartconferences
 .precisionglobalcon.com/abstract-submission.php\n🔗 Register Now:\nhttps
 ://www.heartconferences.precisionglobalcon.com/registration.php\n📧 Cont
 act Us:\nheart@pgconferences.com\nOrganizer\nPrecision Global Conferences\
 n📍 601 King St Ste 200 #863\, Alexandria\, VA 22314\, United States\n
 📞 +1-571-556-1014\n📩 heart@precisionglobalconferences.com
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/heart-world-conference-2026-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Howard Jones & Special Guests - Things Can Only Get Better Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260823T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260823T230000
UID:blogto-233783@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/17/original_imagec23aa948-1e64-4d36-97c3-b136a60629
 2f.jpg
DESCRIPTION:HOWARD JONES\nTHINGS CAN ONLY GET BETTER TOUR\nWITH WANG CHUNG
 \, THE ENGLISH BEAT\, MODERN ENGLISH & RICHARD BLADE\nElectronic music pio
 neer Howard Jones has been a constant presence on the international tourin
 g scene for the past four decades\, playing live in a number of different 
 configurations including intimate solo shows and dates with his full high-
 tech band set-up. He first burst upon the contemporary music scene in 1983
 \, with his very English songwriting and pioneering synthesizers with “N
 ew Song”. His first two albums HUMAN’S LIB and DREAM INTO ACTION were 
 worldwide hits. HUMAN’S LIB reached #1 in 1984in the UK and featured the
  hits “New Song\,” and “What Is Love?”In 1985\, Jones released the
  follow-up\, DREAM INTO ACTION\, which quickly became a Top Ten Platinum a
 lbum in the United States and featured the smashes: “Things Can Only Get
  Better\,” “Life In One Day\,” “No One Is To Blame\,” and “Lik
 eTo Get To Know You Well.” Howard Jones has sold upwards of 10 million a
 lbums worldwide and continues to make new music and tour the world. Jones 
 has performed on NBC’s top-rated morning and nighttime shows respectivel
 y\, Today and The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon. His ubiquitous hits 
 can be heard in such high-profile television series and films such as “S
 tranger Things\,” “Breaking Bad\,” “Watchmen\,” “The Carrie Di
 aries”\,“Superstore” and “Bumblebee”. Howard Jones’ most recen
 t album is DIALOGUE\, which was released in September\, 2022. DIALOGUE is 
 the third album in a trilogy of electronic releases from Jones with multi-
 media project ENGAGE coming out in 2015 and studio album TRANSFORM out in 
 2019. DIALOGUE garnered serious coverage in outlets such as Spin\, Stereog
 um and more.
LOCATION:The Bowl at Sobeys Stadium
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/howard-jones-special-guests-things-can-o
 nly-get-better-tour-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
